1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,488
My tears just paid my electric bill. Do you know what it costs to cry on command?

2
00:00:04,788 --> 00:00:12,684
The city meter reads your grief. Sad thoughts equal soft cash. Happy smiles leave you starving in the dark.

3
00:00:12,984 --> 00:00:19,440
I never felt a damn thing. I just watched old sad movies until my eyes leaked on the scanner.

4
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:27,852
Rent is due tomorrow. The standard heartbreak movie isn't cutting it anymore. My tear ducts are completely dry.

5
00:00:28,152 --> 00:00:36,072
So I invented a tragedy. I imagined the absolute worst thing that could ever possibly happen to me.

6
00:00:36,372 --> 00:00:43,620
I imagined holding someone I loved as they faded away, leaving me utterly alone in this cold world.

7
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:52,656
The scanner beeped instantly. Green light flashed. A flood of currency poured into my digital wallet.

8
00:00:52,956 --> 00:00:58,908
I was rich. I could finally eat. But then I looked at the security camera footage on the wall.

9
00:00:59,208 --> 00:01:06,000
The system didn't pay me for faking. It paid me because for one second, I believed my own lie.

10
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:13,092
I bought my dinner with a manufactured soul. If your sorrow buys survival, are you even human anymore?
